body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

In `packetMembership`, the loop iterates over `nextWaveWorkPackets?.packets`. If any element in the packets array is null or undefined, accessing `packet.rows` directly will throw a `TypeError` and crash the script. Adding a null/undefined guard at the beginning of the loop prevents unhandled exceptions.

```suggestion
function packetMembership(questionKey, nextWaveWorkPackets) {
  for (const packet of asArray(nextWaveWorkPackets?.packets)) {
    if (!packet) continue;
    const packetRows = asArray(packet.rows);
    const index = packetRows.findIndex((row) => row?.question_key === questionKey);
    if (index !== -1) {
      return {
        packet_id: packet.packet_id ?? null,
        packet_row_index: index,
        packet_rank_start: packet.packet_rank_start ?? null,
        packet_rank_end: packet.packet_rank_end ?? null,
      };
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```

