In `countBlockerClasses`, the mapping function `(blocker) => blocker.blocker_class` directly accesses `blocker_class` without optional chaining. If any blocker in the array is null or undefined, this will throw a `TypeError`. Using optional chaining `blocker?.blocker_class` makes the mapping safe.

```suggestion
function countBlockerClasses(rows) {
  const counts = new Map();
  for (const row of rows) {
    const classes = new Set(asArray(row.blockers).map((blocker) => blocker?.blocker_class).filter(Boolean));
    for (const blockerClassValue of classes) {
      counts.set(blockerClassValue, (counts.get(blockerClassValue) ?? 0) + 1);
    }
  }
  return Object.fromEntries([...counts.entries()].sort(([left], [right]) => compareNatural(left, right)));
}
